    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but wouldn't you agree that \"challenging the status quo\" is often just a way for artists to push a specific partisan agenda? it feels like there's a big difference between art that makes you think and art that's just trying to lecture you on what to believe politically. doesn't that shift the role of the artist from a creator to basically a political activist?",
